;; world/rooms/wrongwater/x-3y8.room
(room
  region: wrongwater
  at: (-3 8)
  title: "Stepping Lakes"
  intent: "three small lakes hang at different heights, and the way up is to choose your lake and swim through it, then the next"
  bed: (air 0.15 water 0.5 hang 0.6 drone 0.6)
  light: 0.6
  grid:
  ("#########%  %############"
   "##########~~~############"
   "##########~~~############"
   "###                  ####"
   "###                  ####"
   "###~~~####   #####~~~####"
   "###~~~####   #####~~~####"
   "###                      "
   "###                      "
   "#########################"
   "#########################")
  start: (8 8)
  decor: auto)
;; Two low lakes, each walled on both sides, bottoms two rows over the floor
;; (standing row 8): west (3-5) and east (18-20), rows 5-6. They are a
;; scenic route: swim up either and leap out level with its top onto a ledge
;; (west 6-9, east 13-17, standing row 4), but the ledges are 4 rows (32 px)
;; over the floor, inside the 52 px held jump, so a plain jump reaches them
;; too (reach probe gh-no-low-lakes passes with both lakes removed). From
;; either ledge's inner edge a jump enters the high lake (10-12, rows 1-2),
;; which fills the shaft and is the only way up: from its top the rough hole
;; (10-11, rough 9 and 12) climbs into the Inverted Fall. Coming down the
;; hole you drop into the high lake and sink out onto the floor. 18 cells of
;; water, all small and walled. East to the Upward Grove (rows 7-8).
